#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# primes

#% text
# `primes` is the domain of the prime numbers: `element(x, primes)` is `true` when `x` is a prime number.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Negative integers, 1 and numbers that are not integers are not in the domain.

#% item
# `element(x, primes)` maps over lists and stays unevaluated for symbols.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
element(107, primes)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element([17, -17, 1, 9, 7/2], primes)
#% output
#= [true, false, false, false, false]

#% cell
element(2^107 - 1, primes)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(a, primes)
#% output
#= element(a, primes)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_prime`, `prime`, `integers`
